      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "\"Stopping participation\" doesn't have to mean quitting your job; it means withdrawing your energy from the performance. You can start by finding a way to make the *inside* of your head yours again, even if the outside remains the same. Think about a small, private act of defiance—something that only you know about, a tiny moment of self-ownership that the machine can't touch.",
      "source": "target",
